  "description": "The proposal seeks to replace the existing timber-framed sash windows and timber French doors at Flats 4, 6, and 7 at Clifton House with matching aluminium-framed sash windows and aluminium French doors. The new units will replicate the original fenestration in terms of design, dimensions, glazing configuration, and opening mechanisms. The aluminium frames will be finished in a colour and profile that matches the existing painted timber, ensuring minimal visual impact and preserving the architectural character of the building.The proposed upgrade aims to enhance glazing thermal performance, reduce long-term maintenance, and improve sustainability, while remaining sensitive to the heritage significance of the conservation area. \n",
